# Stake

Stake is a mental model—a conceptual tool or principle that helps understand and navigate complex situations. It provides a mental shortcut or framework for making sense of patterns and relationships in the world.

## Definition

Stake functions as a universal mental shortcut for navigating complexity via pattern and relationship recognition. It is applicable across general domains and helps make sense of complex situations by identifying key patterns and relationships.

## Cross-Source Perspectives

This mental model is referenced in Nassim Nicholas Taleb's *Skin in the Game*, which emphasizes accountability and having something at risk as a framework for understanding complex systems. The concept overlaps with the broader idea of [[skin-in-the-game]]—the principle that those making decisions should bear the consequences of those decisions.

## Connections

- [[skin-in-the-game]] — Overlapping concept of accountability and risk-bearing
